WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.027
(dramatic music)

00:00:02.027 --> 00:00:05.700
- [Josephine] In 1947, the first
H&amp;M store opened in Sweden.

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:10.020
And by 2019, there were over
5,000 H&amp;Ms around the world,

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:13.170
about 3000 more than its competitor Zara.

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:14.353
- [Interviewer] How long have you waiting

00:00:14.353 --> 00:00:15.651
this morning in the queue?

00:00:15.651 --> 00:00:19.470
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:20.646
- [Josephine] It collaborated
with fashion giants

00:00:20.646 --> 00:00:24.311
like Versace, Balmain, and Karl Lagerfeld.

00:00:24.311 --> 00:00:25.590
(dramatic music)

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:27.270
- [Narrator] The world has changed.

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:30.180
What we do today will define our tomorrow.

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:32.670
- [Josephine] But recently,
H&amp;M has struggled.

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:35.340
The company's net income
dropped during the pandemic.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:38.520
And 2022 was one of the
store's least profitable years

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:39.960
in over two decades.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:43.533
That same year H&amp;M laid
off 1500 employees.

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:46.479
So what went wrong?

00:00:46.479 --> 00:00:47.910
(dramatic music)

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:50.190
- This morning major American
companies pulling business

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:53.730
out of Russia, Disney, Warner
Brothers, ExxonMobil, Ford.

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:56.580
- [Josephine] Russia was
H&amp;Ms sixth largest market.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:58.590
But after Russia invaded Ukraine,

00:00:58.590 --> 00:01:01.470
H&amp;M decided to close all
of its stores in Russia

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:03.330
and stop online sales to the country.

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:05.490
The company cited operational challenges

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:07.290
and an unpredictable future.

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:09.840
- They, of course, faced
this unprecedented situation,

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:13.020
like a lot of brands last
year with Russia's invasion

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:16.290
of Ukraine, that forced them
to close a lot of stores

00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:18.390
in what was one of their bigger markets,

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:20.880
about 5% of their global sales.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:24.240
So H&amp;M would argue that without that hit

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:27.390
they would've had a
fairly decent last year.

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:30.330
- [Helena] So our decision to
wind down the business there

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:34.680
has had a significant negative
impact on our results.

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:36.870
- [Josephine] The war also
helped fuel inflation,

00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:39.570
increasing raw material,
and logistical costs.

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:41.250
Besides pulling out of Russia,

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:44.010
H&amp;M has had longstanding
problems in China,

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:45.908
another important market.

00:01:45.908 --> 00:01:49.825
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:56.760 --> 00:02:00.120
Consumers in China boycotted
the company in 2021

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:03.300
after H&amp;M raised concerns
about alleged forced labor

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:05.460
and discrimination
against ethnic minorities

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:06.960
in China's cotton production.

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:10.513
Chinese consumers and online
retail apps like Tmall,

00:02:10.513 --> 00:02:13.500
Pinduoduo, and JD boycotted H&amp;M.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:17.160
Map apps like Baidu also removed
H&amp;M from their platforms.

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:19.560
- They've never really
recovered from that issue.

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:21.540
They're still trying to find a way back

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:22.920
into the China market.

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:25.890
- [Josephine] H&amp;M also faced
a setback when Covid lockdowns

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:28.293
in China led to store
closures in the country.

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:31.500
- First, I got this hoodie.

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:34.140
I am actually obsessed with this.

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:37.800
- One big factor they face
is their brand position.

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:39.510
They're are a fast fashion brand

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:42.093
so all about being relatively cheap.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:45.510
But in recent years, they've
faced this new competition

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:49.170
from online fast fashion
players, like SHEIN,

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:53.460
who are even cheaper, even
quicker to get new designs

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:54.660
onto the market.

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:55.800
- [Josephine] SHEIN has
come onto the market

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:58.470
as one of H&amp;Ms fast fashion competitors.

00:02:58.470 --> 00:03:02.040
And unlike H&amp;M, SHEIN is
an online only retailer.

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:04.440
- They don't have physical
stores, that's their model.

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:05.430
- [Josephine] On the other hand,

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:08.430
H&amp;M relies heavily on in-store sales.

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:11.490
Only about 30% of its
sales come from online.

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:16.140
- So H&amp;M faces this predicament
that on the low side,

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:19.530
they're being out flanked
by SHEIN and online players.

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:20.760
But do you try and trade up?

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:22.920
Because if you do, then you are coming

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:25.230
into direct competition
with a brand like Zara,

00:03:25.230 --> 00:03:27.930
which in the mind of a lot of consumers

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:29.850
is a slightly higher end brand.

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:32.250
They've already closed something like 12%

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:34.050
of their global stores.

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:36.630
And analysts generally think
that's the right way to go.

00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:39.000
That you close the underperforming stores,

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:41.280
invest in the best stores
because most consumers

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:43.620
still like to shop in physical stores,

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:46.170
but then also try and build
up the digital side as well.

00:03:46.170 --> 00:03:48.210
- [Josephine] But can
H&amp;M get customers excited

00:03:48.210 --> 00:03:49.440
about the brand again?

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:51.240
- Fashion is a tricky business, of course,

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:53.610
'cause it relies a lot on
this sort of intangible idea

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:56.220
of brand heat and whether your brand

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:57.780
resonates with consumers.

00:03:57.780 --> 00:04:00.660
And H&amp;M seems to have lost a
little bit of that resonance

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:01.740
with a lot of consumers.

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:05.250
Can they get consumers excited again

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:08.040
about H&amp;M clothes at the
price point they're at?

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:11.010
And at the moment they, maybe
they're having some success,

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:13.380
but I think they'd like to see a lot more

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:17.398
to really get young consumers
especially back on board.

00:04:17.398 --> 00:04:20.148
(dramatic music)

